From: Khem Raj <raj.khem@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ld.hugetlbfs: Add riscv64 support

riscv64 was added to the Makefiles in 2.23, but ld.hugetlbfs has no
case for its elf64lriscv emulation, so HPAGE_SIZE and SLICE_SIZE stay
empty. Linking the HTLB_ALIGN=slice tests then passes
"-zcommon-page-size= -zmax-page-size=", which LLD rejects:

  ld.lld: error: invalid max-page-size:

riscv64 uses 2MB (PMD) huge pages by default. Like aarch64, set the
text segment address explicitly: with a 2MB max page size the default
image base would otherwise be aligned down to 0.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/libhugetlbfs/libhugetlbfs/pull/119]
Signed-off-by: Khem Raj <raj.khem@gmail.com>
---
 ld.hugetlbfs | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/ld.hugetlbfs
+++ b/ld.hugetlbfs
@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@ armelf*_linux_eabi|aarch64elf*|aarch64li
 	hpage_kb=$(cat /proc/meminfo  | grep Hugepagesize: | awk '{print $2}')
 	HPAGE_SIZE=$((hpage_kb * 1024))
 	SLICE_SIZE=$HPAGE_SIZE ;;
+elf64lriscv*)		HPAGE_SIZE=$((2*$MB)) SLICE_SIZE=$HPAGE_SIZE ;;
 esac
 
 # LLD does not implement -Ttext-segment, --image-base is its equivalent
@@ -136,7 +137,7 @@ if [ "$HTLB_ALIGN" == "slice" ]; then
 	# targeting the ARM platform one needs to explicitly set the text segment offset
 	# otherwise it will be NULL.
 	case "$EMU" in
-	armelf*_linux_eabi|aarch64elf*|aarch64linux*)
+	armelf*_linux_eabi|aarch64elf*|aarch64linux*|elf64lriscv*)
 		printf -v TEXTADDR "0x%x" "$SLICE_SIZE"
 		HTLBOPTS="$HTLBOPTS ${TEXTSEG}$TEXTADDR" ;;
 	elf_i386)		HTLBOPTS="$HTLBOPTS ${TEXTSEG}0x08000000" ;;
